{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1492170-ghostheart-implementation","id":1492170,"title":"Ghostheart Implementation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-02T10:18:06-07:00","id":1492170,"title":"Ghostheart Implementation","content":"Ghostheart is one of my favorite kiths from Kith and Kin, but I'm not sure how I would mechanically implement the option to have one-dot/ two-dot/ three-dot ghosts.<br /> <br /> Dots in the Allies merit normally represent the character's influence over a group, from small favors to stretching the organization to its very limits. So one way to interpret it is that the ghosts are all the same power, and the difference between a three-dot and one-dot ghost is just the kinds of favors that it will do. That might be the easiest to implement, but also seems a little at odds with the wording (three-dot ghost seems to imply a stronger ghost, and the dots represent ghosts the changeling &quot;<b>controls</b> or with whom she's close,&quot; which is a lot more influence than 3 dots of allies). <br /> <br /> The other option is to say that a 3-dot ghost is more powerful. That's more intuitive to me, but I don't know how I would implement it. My first thought was 1 dot in Rank/Wyrd per level, but a rank 3 ghost has 15-25 attribute dots with a max trait score of 9, which is... a lot. I guess it's somewhat balanced by each ghost only having 1 Numen, so you can have access to up to three Numina with low-attribute ghosts, or as few as 1 Numen with a super-high attribute ghost?<br /> <br /> How would you implement these in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6927-gillestrilleuze","name":"GillesTrilleuze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T11:04:48-07:00","id":1492173,"title":"","content":"As written, probably, except to strike \u201ccontrol\u201d and make it behave as close to Allies as possible; ghosts that would help you in a pinch, but not be constantly around you. That is, not as familiars.<br /> <br /> I would hesitate to use Hedge Ghosts as allies as they gain extra abilities, but past Rank 1 they are less capable than their mundane world counterparts. It would be thematic. Also I consider Hedge Ghosts to belong to the Hedge, but that\u2019s just my personal take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T12:36:40-07:00","id":1492182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GillesTrilleuze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1492170-ghostheart-implementation#post1492170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghostheart is one of my favorite kiths from Kith and Kin, but I'm not sure how I would mechanically implement the option to have one-dot/ two-dot/ three-dot ghosts.<br /> <br /> Dots in the Allies merit normally represent the character's influence over a group, from small favors to stretching the organization to its very limits. So one way to interpret it is that the ghosts are all the same power, and the difference between a three-dot and one-dot ghost is just the kinds of favors that it will do. That might be the easiest to implement, but also seems a little at odds with the wording (three-dot ghost seems to imply a stronger ghost, and the dots represent ghosts the changeling &quot;<b>controls</b> or with whom she's close,&quot; which is a lot more influence than 3 dots of allies).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason I submitted an erratum suggesting that the writer probably meant Retainers rather than Allies, which then makes the trade number of Numina versus effectiveness as a Retainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}